  "Description": {
    "Cost": 825437,
    "UIName": "Night Stalker",
    "Id": "chassisdef_night_stalker_NSR-K3",
    "Name": "Night Stalker",
    "Details": "One of the most notable attributes of the Night Stalker NSR-K3 is its speed. Powered by its 320 XL extralight engine, the 40 ton design can quickly close distance between it and its objective. In its role as a recon and pursuit 'Mech, the Night Stalker is fitted with a Beagle active probe to find hidden units. Other design features include a torso-mounted cockpit and TAG - the latter of which can be used to call in artillery support. Protecting the 'Mech's hull are six and a half tons of ferro-fibrous armor. The Night Stalker's arsenal is meant for intermediate and close-in fighting, with a pair of right arm-mounted ER medium lasers and an SRM-6 in the left torso. Upon entering close range, the 'Mech can bring its ER small laser and small pulse laser to bear on a potential target. In combination with the Night Stalker' speed, a MechWarrior can use its unusually-shaped left arm-mounted lance to pierce an enemy's armor.\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Quirk: Distracting</color></b>\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Drop Cost Multiplier: 1.02</color></b>",
    "Icon": "uixTxrIcon_nightstalker"
  },
  "VariantName": "NSR-K3",
  "ChassisTags": {
